scope: |
  Planned. The claim was widened after reading the code, and the reason is the plan:
  the static-frontend path CANNOT EXPRESS a signal-URL fetch at all, so this is not an
  emitter-only change. FetchUrlSignal carries `fetchUrl: String` with no `urlId`, and the
  v1 fetch-plugin implements `fetchUrlSignal` but has no `fetchUrlSignalTo` site — that
  primitive exists only in the JS runtime and v2's UiNativePlugin. So:
    1. Primitives.scala — FetchUrlSignal gains `urlId: Option[String]`, mirroring the
       `headersId` that tui-fetch-headers just added; `fetchUrl` stays as the static form.
    2. FetchIntrinsics.scala — a `fetchUrlSignalTo` site that builds it.
    3. TuiEmitter — resolve the URL from the signal store at FETCH time and re-fetch when
       it changes, exactly as the tick already does (and as headers now do).
    4. TuiEmitterTest — the gate.
  Additive for every other static emitter: an ignored Option field.
next: cargo integration tests for both — BLOCKED on TuiCargoSmokeTest.scala (tui-widget-compile-coverage); asked in the room, will land them the moment that claim releases or its holder says go
note: |
